DESCRIPTION:Topic: Lessons Learned from a Cyber Attack: Toronto Public Lib
 rary’s Experience\n\nOn October 28\, 2023\, Toronto Public Library shut 
 down every network and computer system wide after discovering a cyberattac
 k\, meanwhile all 100 branches remained open anyway. This session walks th
 rough the incident response governance\, the phased restoration of a 5\,00
 0+ computer environment\, and the lessons TPL is willing to share so other
  public sector organizations don't learn them the hard way.\n\nSpeaker: St
 eve Till-Rogers (he/him)\n\nSteve Till-Rogers is the Director of Digital S
 trategy and Chief Information Officer with the Toronto Public Library. TPL
  is Canada’s largest public library with 100 branches located throughout
  Toronto. Steve leads delivery of TPL’s Digital Strategy executing IT se
 rvice modernization\, innovation and enhancing digital access.\n\nPrior to
  joining Toronto Public Library\, Steve was the Director of Technology Ser
 vices with Edmonton Public Library. During his time at EPL\, Steve deploye
 d new technologies and digital experiences within the library including Th
 e Wall\, at the Stanley A. Milner Library.\n\nPreviously named as a Digita
 l Game Changer by HP Enterprise\, Steve is recognized for his expertise in
  digital infrastructure\, integrated systems\, and leveraging technology t
 o enhance library services and patron experiences. ‎‎‎\n\nAgenda:\n\
 n7:00-7:20 Welcome and Introductions\n\n7:20-7:50 Presentation and Q\\&A/d
